<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Use the mid-ordinate rule with <m>{4}</m> strips to estimate the area bounded by <m>y = {3 x^2+2 x+3}</m>, the <m>x</m>-axis and the lines <m>x = {1}</m> and <m>x = {3}</m>. Give exact values.</p><p>(a) What is the strip width <m>h</m>?</p><div><m>h =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) At what value of <m>x</m> is the first mid-ordinate?</p><div><m>x =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/>  </div><p>(c) Find the mid-ordinate estimate of the area.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans3"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) <m>h = \dfrac{ {3} - {1} }{ {4} } = {0.5}</m>.</p><p>(b) The height at the middle of a strip stands for the whole strip. The first strip runs from <m>x = {1}</m> to <m>x = {1.5}</m>, so its middle is at <m>x = {1} + \tfrac{1}{2} \times {0.5} = {1.25}</m>.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Middle <m>x</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1.25}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1.75}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2.25}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{2.75}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Mid-ordinate <m>m</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10.188}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{15.688}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{22.688}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{31.188}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>(c) <m>M = h(m_1 + \cdots + m_{ {4} }) = {0.5} \times {79.75} = {39.875}</m>.</p><p>For comparison, the trapezoidal rule with the same strips gives <m>{40.25}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{1}{2}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{5}{4}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{319}{8}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>